@node C1 "wHAT iS SStatus ???"
                        #-----------------------#
                        |  wHAT iS SStatus ???  |
                        #-----------------------#

                   SStatus is simply a Status Door.
                     It replaces the "S" command!

            The specialy of this door is that it is aNIMATED!!!

             This door is realy fast because it's coded as XIM!

                               That's it!
@endnode
@node C2 "wHAT u nEED !!!"
                           #-----------------#
                           | wHAT u nEED !!! |
                           #-----------------#

                                 U need:

          1. Of course an Amiga! It should be run on every Amiga!

                       2. AmiExpress. Minimum /X 2.x

          3. The following files min. contained in this archive:

                        - SStatus.exe (mainfile)
                        - s.info (the "S" replacement)
                        - SStatus.guide (this document)
@endnode
@node C3 "hOW tO iNSTALL ???"
                          #--------------------#
                          | hOW tO iNSTALL ??? |
                          #--------------------#

      1. Copy the directorys named: STD/SStatus/ into your Doors:

     2a. If u use /X3.x copy the t.info in your: BBS:Commands/BBSCMD/

     2b. If u use /X2.x copy the following to your: BBS:Commands/BBS.CMD

------------------Cut here------------------
T         XM005DOORS:STD/SStatus/SStatus.exe
------------------Cut here------------------
@endnode
@node C4 "hOW tO uSE ???"
                           #----------------#
                           | hOW tO uSE ??? |
                           #----------------#

                    There is nothing specialy to know!
           U have only to call the door and then... LOOK AROUND!

               The only what I could tell you are the @{" aRGS " LINK C5}
@endnode
@node C5 "aRGS"
                                 #------#
                                 | aRGS |
                                 #------#

                       But there is only 1 argument!

                                TYPE: "S ?"

                                    @{" ? " LINK C7}
@endnode
